origin_server_channel.description:
Name of the channel in `origin_server` it came from, for a copy from another server whose
sender chose to show where it is from, when everyone in that server may see the channel;
`null` otherwise. Copies inside one server use `origin_channel`.

oneOf.description:
The member's running timeout. Only in `GET /api/v1/servers/{name}/members` and `GET
/api/v1/servers/{name}/members/search` for callers with the Timeout members permission;
absent otherwise and when none is running.

profile_locked_until.description:
Until when (unix seconds) a moderator locked the user's server profile;
9223372036854775807 for a lock that stays until it is lifted. Only for viewers with the
Reset server profiles permission; absent otherwise and when it is not locked.

avatar_image.description:
The id of the profile picture uploaded for this server (see `UserRef.avatar_image`);
`null` without one. It shows over the avatar of this look, or over the account's when
`avatar_kind` is `null`. A look with an `avatar_kind` and no picture shows no picture.

oneOf.description:
For a message posted through an incoming webhook, the webhook and its rich embeds;
`null` otherwise. `author` then carries the name and avatar the webhook posted with (its
`username` is `@webhook:<id>`, which no account can have). Clients show a WEBHOOK badge.

sha256.description:
SHA-256 of the file's bytes as 64 hexadecimal characters (stored lowercase), computed
when attaching it. Recipients check downloads against it. Optional for older clients;
files without it are shown as unverified.

profile_locked_until.description:
Until when (unix seconds) a moderator locked the user's server profile;
9223372036854775807 for a lock that stays until it is lifted. Only for viewers with the
Reset server profiles permission; absent otherwise and when it is not locked.

icon_image.description:
The id of the server's uploaded picture, served at `GET /api/v1/avatars/{id}/{size}`;
`null` without one. The icon of `icon_kind` shows until it has loaded and where pictures
are not shown. Set with `PUT /api/v1/servers/{name}/icon`.

public_read.description:
"Anyone can read this server", as in `PATCH /api/v1/servers/{name}`: `true` or `false`;
omit to follow the instance. `true` is refused while the instance's `public_reading` is
off.

icon_image.description:
The id of the server's uploaded picture, served at `GET /api/v1/avatars/{id}/{size}`;
`null` without one. The icon of `icon_kind` shows until it has loaded and where pictures
are not shown. Set with `PUT /api/v1/servers/{name}/icon`.

